	)
	(text "TLV7044_U5"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.015 47.625 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "91c17334-74ef-417d-a5f5-8648006cf8e6")
	)
	(text "RV1 selects the leak reference:\n	RV1 sets V_Leak_ref (0 - VDD*2/3)\n	U1D buffers this into a low-impedance V_Leak\n\nThe leak branch sets the passive membrane pull:\n	V_Leak is connected to Vm_Int through the adjustable leak path\n	→ Creates a current proportional to (V_Leak - Vm_Int)\n\nWhen Vm_Int is below V_Leak:\n	→ Leak current flows into the membrane node\n	→ Vm_Int is pulled upward toward V_Leak\n\nWhen Vm_Int is above V_Leak:\n Leak current flows out of the membrane node\n Vm_Int is pulled downward toward V_Leak\n\nLIF AdEx model:\n	Implements the passive leak term\n	𝐼𝐿𝑒𝑎𝑘 = 𝑔𝐿.(𝐸𝐿−𝑉𝑚)\n 	where V_Leak is the analog equivalent of E_L\n 	and the leak branch sets the effective g_L."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 233.68 248.285 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "93674d3c-8ae5-41e1-8c70-c5ada7c29c69")
	)
	(text "RV6-9 set the signed synapse level:  \n	The pot spans from GNDREF to V_Leak_Ref_Max  \n	→ Its midpoint corresponds to V_Leak, so the channel is neutral at mid setting\n	→ Above midpoint the synapse is excitatory \n	→ Below midpoint the synapse is inhibitory\n\nIncoming spikes gate the channel:\n	The external spike input is conditioned and clamped to the local logic domain\n	When the switch closes, V_Syn*_Set is applied  to V_Syn_State\n\n\n\nV_Syn_State decays back to V_Leak:\n	RV5 + R77 and C36 set the synaptic decay time course\n	U2C buffers the state node so membrane loading does not disturb the decay\n\nThe buffered synapse state injects current into the membrane:\n	Through R78, the synapse drives Vm_Int with a depolarising or hyperpolarising current depending on whether V_Syn_State is above or below V_Leak\n\n\n\nLIF AdEx model:\n	Implements a simplified signed synaptic input.\n	Each presynaptic spike produces a transient synaptic state that decays back to baseline, and this state injects excitatory or inhibitory current into the membrane."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 668.02 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9561de91-a10c-4688-be2f-f6dd4fc969c9")
	)
	(text "Vsel chooses one membrane-capacitance state:  \n	The threshold ladder and comparator windows generate one active select line at a time  \n	Each select line closes one analog switch and connects its capacitor to Vm_Int\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 279.4 127 0)
		(effects
